## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic SwiftUI parity of the web `LiveTelemetryPanels` composition (the "Live Telemetry" section header + responsive 2-column grid of 7 staggered panels: Powertrain, Climate, Security, Vehicle State, Tire Pressure, Energy & Charging, Media & Navigation).

**Capability finding:** SwiftUI/Swift Charts/MapKit are available via the macOS SDK, but the runner has **only Command Line Tools** — no full Xcode and no iOS Simulator (`simctl` absent). So the `xcodebuild build test` gate steps are environment-**DEFERRED** (real `IOS_EXIT=1`/`MAC_EXIT=1` captured), matching the established disposition of prior P4 Apple surfaces.

**14 files** (canonical convention, each ≤400 lines): `.swift`, `.Adapter`, `.Snapshots`, `.Projection`, `.ProjectionMedia`, `.Model`, `.Views`, `.Panels`, `.PanelsState`, `.PanelsMedia`, `.Previews`, `.strings`, `.Tests`, `.ModelTests`.

**Every host-runnable gate is genuinely green:**
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| Full macOS `swiftc -typecheck` (real SwiftUI + shared Components/Design tree, strict concurrency) | **EXIT=0** |
| Isolated SwiftPM build + **executed** assertion harness (XCTest/Swift Testing unavailable on CLT) | **124/124 passed** |
| `swiftc -parse` of the two XCTest files | **EXIT=0** |
